From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:07:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kk: unroll direct non-indexed draws on the CPU; name what a
 failed command buffer contained

STEAMAC-G. A draw whose fragment shader reads a flat varying with the last
vertex provoking (zink keeps GL's) is unrolled into indices that rotate the
last vertex first. The unroll kernel ended the render pass around every such
draw: the attachments stored, a compute pass, the attachments loaded again.
Steam's web helper composites its first frame that way, 12 rectangles into
its LINEAR window buffer (host memory): 13 render passes over the whole
2560x1600 window, 43 ms of GPU time on an M1 Max, about a second after Steam's
hellovr_vulkan probe, which is where M3 and later GPUs lost the device (its
command buffer a victim of the GPU's recovery after 50-120 ms, another one
blamed with Hang). Direct draws without an index buffer now get the same
indices written by the CPU at recording (indexed indirect draws from the
command buffer's upload memory, as the kernel wrote them): one render pass,
0.37 ms instead of 27 ms for 11 such draws into a 2560x1600 LINEAR host import.

Command queue error diagnostics: command buffers keep a record of what they
encoded (render passes and how many multisampled, compute encoders, draws and
dispatches with the indirect ones, KosmicKrisp operations: meta clears,
blits, resolves, copies, fills, query resets/copies, queries, timestamps,
events, GS/tessellation passes, conditional rendering; the libkk kernels; the
MSL hashes of the programs bound, with L/D/S/A/B/W features: loops, discard,
SIMD-group/quad operations, atomics, barriers, texture writes). The queue
keeps the records of its last 16 commits and their outcome (the IOGPU reason
parsed from the error's userInfo: Hang, InnocentVictim, ...). A failure
prints its command buffer's record; the first one in the process also waits
up to 300 ms for the feedback of every command buffer of every device still
on the GPU and names them with their outcome and GPU time (the one that hung
is blamed "Hang", the others are victims), then logs an excerpt of the MSL of
programs with loops, atomics or barriers of the ones that hung. Reading
os_log is dropped: its IOGPU and Metal warning messages are <private>, the
rest repeated the userInfo, and its 2-4 s delayed the device loss line past
other devices' failures. MESA_KK_DEBUG=cbs logs every command buffer's record
and outcome; MESA_KK_DEBUG=msl prints each MSL's hash.
---
